{"type":"session/learning-request","data":{"turn":1,"route":{"provider":"deepseek-official","model":"deepseek-v4-pro"},"system":"You review one finished turn of an AI coding-assistant session and extract knowledge worth keeping for later work on this machine and project.\nKeep durable items: environment facts (paths, tool versions, commands that work), shortcuts and workarounds that were discovered, explicit user preferences, and lessons from the work: the root cause of a problem once it was established, an approach that failed and why, a wrong assumption that was corrected, and a decision the user made.\nWrite every item so it can be checked against a later task: name its situation (the file, command, component, or problem it is about) so it is never applied to a different case that only shares a word.\nDo not keep plans or progress reports, errors that were never explained, or anything the repository already documents.\nAnswer with a JSON array only. Each item is {\"text\": string, \"kind\": \"fact\" | \"shortcut\" | \"preference\", \"tags\": string[]}; a lesson is a \"fact\" tagged \"lesson\". Text is one or two sentences. Return [] when nothing qualifies.","messages":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract reusable knowledge from this turn transcript:\nuser: Exercise the six PTY tools in order, including one missing-session signal error, then reply DONE.\ncontext: Current runtime context. This snapshot supersedes earlier runtime-context snapshots. Current DSH file policy: danger-full-access. The DSH file sandbox does not restrict file modifications by available operations. Approval prompts are disabled in this session: actions that require approval are rejected automatically — do not request sandbox escalation (do not set `sandbox_permissions`).\nassistant: \ntool terminal_open: {\"type\":\"shell\",\"name\":\"main\"}\nresult: \nassistant: \ntool terminal_read: {\"sessionId\":\"pty-1\",\"offset\":0,\"count\":20}\nresult: \nassistant: \ntool terminal_signal: {\"sessionId\":\"pty-missing\",\"signal\":\"SIGINT\"}\nresult: \nassistant: \ntool terminal_close: {\"sessionId\":\"pty-1\"}\nresult: \nassistant: \ntool terminal_list: {}\nresult: \nassistant: DONE"}],"source":{"kind":"plugin","plugin":"dsh-learning"},"role":"user","id":"{{message:15}}"}],"maxTokens":512},"ignorable":true}
